\par
He\rquote s crazy, Layla realized. It was something she had somehow forgotten. Yes, Duke Herhardt is out of his mind.\par
\ldblquote Aren\rquote t you going to answer?\rdblquote  he asked, smiling.\par
He was clutching her hair with a relatively gentle grip, compared to the ferocity with which he had just chased her to the willow tree. She was too frightened and humiliated to notice this, however.\par
\ldblquote Layla,\rdblquote  he said in an even quieter voice.\par
She tried to back away from him, but the tree trunk behind her blocked her way. Despite the speed with which he had just been running, he had already caught his breath. She, on the other hand, was still panting. Each time her chest rose and fell, she could feel the proximity of his large, strong body more vividly, which only added to her embarrassment.\par
\par
\ldblquote Why are you\'85\rdblquote  she said in a trembling voice as she used all her might to try to push his shoulders away. \ldblquote Why are you doing this to me?\rdblquote  Realizing that her strength wasn\rquote t enough to push him away, she tried to twist out of his grip.\par
Amused by her futile attempts, Matthias pressed his body firmly against hers. He smiled even more contently as he felt her body freeze with fear.\par
\ldblquote I want you to answer me, not ask another question.\rdblquote  He looked straight into her scowling eyes. \ldblquote Answer me, Layla.\rdblquote\par
He slowly caressed her hair. Its soft, smooth texture seemed to soothe the displeasure he had been feeling all week long. It even made her lack of response feel tolerable.\par
\ldblquote Do you think it\rquote s ladylike of you to neither write me back nor answer my question?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Layla?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Layla Llewellyn.\rdblquote  His grip on her hair gradually tightened.\par
Overcome by an ominous feeling, she finally replied in anger, \ldblquote I don\rquote t know what you\rquote re talking about!\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Didn\rquote t you get my note?\rdblquote  \ldblquote I don\rquote t know.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Layla, you\rquote d better think carefully before speaking.\rdblquote  His smile intensified as he noted the uneasiness in her eyes. \ldblquote If that worthless messenger pigeon couldn\rquote t deliver a single message, what do you think I\rquote ll do with it?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Y-you promised!\rdblquote  she shouted. \ldblquote You promised not to shoot Phoebe!\rdblquote  \ldblquote Did I?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Your Grace!\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Now I\rquote m the one who doesn\rquote t know what you\rquote re talking about,\rdblquote  he said with a mischievous grin. If she was going to blatantly lie, he saw no reason why he shouldn\rquote t lie back to her.\par
\par
She briefly glared at him before lowering her quivering eyelids. \ldblquote I\rquote m sorry\'85\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote For what?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote You already know.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote For ignoring my note, for running away, or for lying?\rdblquote\par
She flinched as he pointed out each of her misdeeds. He liked that she was becoming more docile, but he didn\rquote t like that he couldn\rquote t see her eyes.\par
\ldblquote That\rquote s enough with the apologies,\rdblquote  he said, raising her chin with his index finger.\par
He was handling her face like it was a delicate, fragile object. This made her quiver with fear. He didn\rquote t mind this reaction. The satisfaction he felt from their restored eye contact made up for the slight bitterness he was feeling.\par
\ldblquote I guess that pen meant nothing to you, since you don\rquote t seem to care that you lost it.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote No, it means a lot to me! But\'85\rdblquote\par
She trailed off and tried to turn her head away from him, but he gripped her chin to keep her facing him.\par
\ldblquote But?\rdblquote  he replied. He didn\rquote t want their conversation to end any more than he wanted her to avoid his gaze.\par
With her hair and chin firmly in his grasp, she let out a resigned sigh and said, \ldblquote I really don\rquote t understand you.\rdblquote\par
Her calm, emerald-colored eyes reflected his image. They were beautiful eyes. They made him think of an eternal summer.\par
\ldblquote Why do you keep stealing my things?\rdblquote  she asked.\par
He raised his eyebrows in reaction to her accusatory question. He knew that she was the only person in Karlsbar, if not in the entire empire, who\par
\par
would dare to talk to him like he was a petty thief. He was so flabbergasted he couldn\rquote t help but chuckle.\par
\ldblquote Are you\'85 a raven?\rdblquote  she asked, scowling at his jet-black hair and his blue eyes.\par
\ldblquote A raven?\rdblquote  he asked with a puzzled expression on his face.\par
She kept speaking her mind. \ldblquote You\rquote re always stealing my\'85 that is, you\rquote re the one who\rquote s in the wrong, so I don\rquote t understand why I should be the one to go to you and beg you to give me my things back every time. It\rquote s not fair.\rdblquote\par
Her voice was steadily rising as she grew angrier. He was happy to hear it. \ldblquote Is that why you didn\rquote t reply to my note?\rdblquote  he asked, smirking.\par
Suddenly she felt foolish, and was at a loss for words. She had gathered all her courage to rebut him, but he had dismissed her with a single derisive question.\par
Just when she was about to speak again, he cut her off. \ldblquote Layla.\rdblquote\par
Her combativeness had disappeared and been replaced by a strange, hard- to- describe feeling. She quickly lowered her eyes as she struggled to think of what to say.\par
\ldblquote Layla,\rdblquote  he said a little more slowly, as if he were humming a tune.\par
She turned her head to the side and her ear touched against his chest. She heard the faint sound of his heart beating. She worried that he might be able to hear her heart beating as well.\par
She pressed her pale hands against his shoulders again. She knew it was no use, but she felt she had to try something.\par
When he finally took a step back to humor her, she let out the breath she had been holding. She was timid but daring, docile but nasty. These contradictions only made her more fascinating to him, and more enticing.\par
\par
\ldblquote Please give me back my pen,\rdblquote  she said.\par
He laughed. She never disappoints. \ldblquote I don\rquote t have it,\rdblquote  he calmly replied. \ldblquote I threw it away.\par
\ldblquote You WHAT ?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I figured you didn\rquote t need it, since you didn\rquote t come looking for it.\rdblquote  \ldblquote Then why did you come to the cottage\'85?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I felt I needed to tell you, Layla,\rdblquote  he said, shrugging. \ldblquote I\rquote m a gentleman, after all.\rdblquote  Still clutching her hair, he started to caress it again. \ldblquote I\rquote m the greatest gentleman in Karlsbar, as even you have acknowledged, Miss Llewellyn.\rdblquote\par
He loosened his grip and her hair spilled down onto her shoulders. She took a step back, glaring at him. Before she could take another step, however, she let out a pained yelp.\par
He had suddenly grabbed the last lock of her hair before it could slip through his fingers.\par
\ldblquote Am I not?\rdblquote  he asked, looking with delight at her eyes filling up with tears from the pain.\par
He\rquote s crazy, she thought again as she struggled to get her hair out of his grip. Grinning, he started playing with the end of the hair he was holding.\par
I can\rquote t believe this guy is the head of the House of Herhardt! As she started to worry about Arvis\rquote s future, she stumbled backward. He had suddenly let go of her hair. She heard the sound of his laughter as she fell to the ground, and then everything went black.\par
When she regained consciousness, his face was right in front of her again. Only when she felt his arm wrapped around her waist did she realize that he was holding her in his embrace.\par
Should I bite him? she thought, feeling like a cornered mouse, when suddenly he let her go.\par
\par
The slyly indifferent look on his face made her shudder.\par
She quickly ran to the edge of the stream. He remained where he stood, calmly checking his wristwatch.\par
\ldblquote I take back what I said,\rdblquote  she shouted. \ldblquote You\rquote re not a gentleman. Not at all!\rdblquote  \ldblquote Suddenly you\rquote ve become a harsh critic,\rdblquote  he said, chuckling.\par
Her cheeks flushed red. \ldblquote It\rquote s true.\rdblquote  \ldblquote Ah, is it?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Yes! If you\rquote re a gentleman, I\rquote m a queen!\rdblquote  She hated herself for giving him such servile praise before.\par
He raised his eyebrows and smirked as he fixed his coat\rquote s lapel. Then he bowed deeply to her, as if he were a servant bowing to a queen, before turning and starting to walk away. The exquisite elegance of the gesture filled her with embarrassment.\par
She stared blankly at his back as he receded into the distance. He had chased her down like a wild beast, tormented her, and then humiliated her all the more by bidding her this graceful farewell.\par
\par
