The car was waiting for him when Matthias arrived at the cabin. He got straight in. The irritation and displeasure he had been feeling when he had left the cabin were completely gone now.\par
The car gathered speed as it drove down the road next to the river. He gazed out the window at the Schulter River for a moment. The slight smile\par
\par
lingering on his face disappeared when turned to look at the documents and letters his assistant had brought for him.\par
To cheer himself up again, he reached into his coat pocket and retrieved the pen.\par
Layla Llewellyn\f1\emdash the gold lettering glittered in the afternoon sun.\par
He slowly ran his fingers over the pen\rquote s glossy surface. He removed the cap, smiling. The sound of the pen scratching against paper filled the sunny interior of the car.\par
\par
\par
