After delivering the rest of the mail to the school, the mailman held out a small package towards Layla. \ldblquote This is for you, Miss Llewellyn.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote For me?\rdblquote  she asked, taking the package. It was strange to be receiving a package at school, rather than at home, and she didn\rquote t recognize the sender\rquote s name or address. \ldblquote Are you sure it\rquote s not a mistake?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Pardon?\rdblquote  He looked closely at the address label. \ldblquote Hmm\'85 No, it\rquote s definitely right.\rdblquote\par
She smiled and shook her head. Despite the unfamiliar sender and address, her name was clearly written on the package.\par
\ldblquote Thank you,\rdblquote  she said before hurrying into the school.\par
It was the newest teacher\rquote s duty to receive and distribute the mail each day. She always started at the principal\rquote s office and went from there to each classroom. By the time she was done distributing all the mail, her break was almost over.\par
\par
She returned to her classroom, sat at her desk, and unwrapped the package she had received. There was a long, narrow box inside, without a note or any other marking.\par
She checked the sender\rquote s name and address again. It was an unfamiliar name, and an unfamiliar city.\par
She cocked her head and opened the box, then looked with wonder at the object inside. It was a black pen with gold trim.\par
The moment she saw it, everything made sense. She knew who had sent it, and for what reason. Her unpleasant memories from the previous weekend came flooding back, and she sighed. The pen looked far more expensive than her original one.\par
She carefully lifted it out of the box. Her named was engraved on the cap, just like it had been on the pen the duke had thrown away.\par
The bell indicating the start of classes rang, and the children swarmed into the classroom.\par
She put the pen back in its box and placed it deep in a drawer of her desk. She hoped that her memories from the weekend would stay there with it, although she knew it was a vain hope.\par
She stepped in front of her podium and smiled brightly. \ldblquote Hello, children.\par
Let\rquote s get started!\rdblquote\par
