The stillness of the dark bedroom was suddenly disturbed by the sound of Phoebe pecking at the window. Normally Layla would have rushed over to the window and opened it, but this time she remained curled up in bed, staring into space. Her slowly blinking eyes looked empty.\par
Several minutes passed before she came out of her daze. It took even longer before she was able to lift herself up out of bed. She didn\rquote t have any cuts or broken bones, but the spots on the left side of her back and shoulder where the car had hit her hurt immensely. She wanted to sleep, but she was in too much pain, and the pain only seemed to be increasing with the passage of time.\par
