As he spoke, his long bangs shook, revealing his deep-blue eyes.\par
\par
Even in the midst of her desperate sobbing, she reflexively shook her head. She hated what Marquess Lindman had done, and she hated that the duke had found out about it. \ldblquote He didn\rquote t touch me\'85 He approached me and was teasing me\'85 so I ran away in fright\'85 That was it.\rdblquote\par
Matthias listened carefully to her faltering words. She started calming down, then started sobbing even more loudly, then calmed down again. Exhausted, she stared into space, sniffling occasionally, her tear- covered face glistening.\par
Still holding down her arms, he gradually slid his hands towards her small hands and gripped them gently.\par
\ldblquote Hold still, Layla.\rdblquote\par
As his fingers slowly interlocked with hers, her slack body flinched and went stiff with fear.\par
Lowering his head slightly, he whispered, \ldblquote I won\rquote t hurt you.\rdblquote\par
She quietly considered the situation she was in. There was a man on top of her. She was being firmly held down by him. The two of them were alone in a remote cabin by the river. She considered trying to push him off of her and making a dash for the door, but quickly realized she wouldn\rquote t be able to escape. This only intensified the despair she was feeling.\par
\ldblquote Really\'85?\rdblquote  she asked, even though she knew she sounded foolish.\par
At this moment, as ridiculous as it seemed, her only hope was the duke. He had now completely let go of her hands and was just looking at her. Her only hope was that he might show her some slight mercy.\par
When he didn\rquote t answer her question, she looked at him with an earnest look in her eyes. She had stopped crying, but her moist eyelashes were still quivering.\par
\par
He gazed at her face for a while longer, then nodded his head. She breathed a sigh of relief.\par
He reached into his jacket pocket and retrieved his handkerchief. Even though her arms were now free, she remained still, staring intently at him in the hopes that he would remember his promise.\par
He slowly started to wipe the tears from her face with the handkerchief. Startled, she tried to turn away, but he grabbed her chin and made her stay facing him. Her emerald eyes looked even more beautiful moistened like this.\par
He wiped the sweat from her forehead and hairline, then he got off of her and stood up. After lying still as a corpse while she endured him wiping her face, she now cautiously shifted her gaze.\par
He picked up a box from the bedside table and turned towards her. It was a first-aid kit. \ldblquote Let me see your wounds,\rdblquote  he said as he sat down on the edge of the bed.\par
She shook her head. \ldblquote It\rquote s okay. I\rquote m not injured.\rdblquote  \ldblquote You said you were hurting.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote That was because\'85\rdblquote  She trailed off and averted her eyes.\par
Rather than make her turn towards him again, he undid the button on one of the sleeves of her blouse, and swiftly rolled the sleeve up past her elbow. She flailed her arm to try to get him to stop.\par
\ldblquote I guess it\rquote s not your arm, then,\rdblquote  he said in a flat tone. He then grasped the hem of her skirt, which was already above her knees, and made as if he were about to pull it up further.\par
\ldblquote My b-back! It\rquote s my back that hurts!\rdblquote  she urgently shouted, afraid that otherwise he would strip her naked to find her wounds. \ldblquote My shoulder and my back are a little hurt. But you don\rquote t need to-\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Take off your blouse,\rdblquote  he said.\par
\par
She sat up in shock and shook her head, but he wasn\rquote t going to take no for an answer.\par
\ldblquote If you don\rquote t want me to see, I\rquote ll call a doctor.\rdblquote  He looked at her with narrowed eyes as he drummed on the first-aid box with his fingers. \ldblquote Dr. Ettman, that is.\rdblquote\par
Upon hearing this, she shook her head even more vehemently. She would rather fling herself into the river than let Kyle\rquote s father see her lying on the duke\rquote s bed in her current state.\par
\ldblquote Make your choice, Layla,\rdblquote  he said in a kind, gentle voice. \ldblquote You can take off your blouse, or you can see Dr. Ettman. It\rquote s up you.\par
