Even though she only had one real option, Layla remained silent for a long while.\par
Matthias gladly waited, despite the tedium. He liked to watch her eyes watching him. They were wet with tears, and yet they were filled with a determination not to cry again. They were beautiful and had a pleading look that contained both trust and fearful doubt.\par
Suddenly, she shut her eyes, and spoke a single word: \ldblquote Promise\'85?\rdblquote\par
The duke would do whatever he wanted to get his way. She knew this well. He had done so many times in the past, and she was sure he would do so now as well. All her attempts to resist would only lengthen the time she had to endure with him, even if this meant enduring the very worst thing he could do.\par
\par
As she felt her utter helplessness anew, she once more burst into tears. Without making any sound this time, she silently shed tears, which flowed down onto her blouse. He continued to sit back and watch her.\par
He must be happy, she thought, seeing me cry again like this. Biting her lip and trying to stifle her sniffles, she turned her back to him. Her tears grew thicker as she started to unbutton her blouse. She wanted to hide the tears from him, even if she could hide nothing else, so she lowered her head as she removed her blouse.\par
It didn\rquote t take long for the smooth fabric to slide down her even smoother skin, but to him, it seemed to take ages. He took in every tiny detail\emdash her fragile, slender neck and shoulders, the soft curve of her spine, and the bruises staining her pale skin.\par
He stared at her bruised, swollen back for a long while. He could see why she had been crying and saying that she was in pain. The dark bruises defiling her white skin ran from her shoulder blade down to her waist.\par
His Adam\rquote s apple twitched as he gulped. He was shocked to the point of pity as he thought about her getting up from the accident in this state and riding her bicycle away.\par
You would have kept these bruises hidden and suffered all by yourself if I had let you, he thought. As he contemplated this, a strong feeling similar to anger welled up inside of him. To rid himself of the emotion, he extended his hand towards her bruise-covered back.\par
She let out a yelp the moment he touched \ldblquote Ah\'85!\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Tell me if there are any spots that hurt more than others,\rdblquote  he said as he tried touching each bone and muscle to check for injuries.\par
Whenever she moaned, he would stop and wait. Fortunately, she was still able to move her shoulders and arms. Her ribs and spine seemed unharmed as\par
\par
well. His wrinkled brow smoothed over with relief as he confirmed this.\par
He thought about saying her name, then changed his mind and wrapped his hand around her left shoulder joint. She was quivering, with her head still lowered.\par
As if he were comforting a small, frightened animal, he gently caressed her bruised body. To the eye, she looked slender enough that he had wondered if she was getting enough to eat, but to the touch, her body felt healthy and supple. Overcome by how small and helpless she seemed, her name quietly escaped his lips: \ldblquote Layla.\rdblquote\par
She flinched and raised her head at the sound of her name. There was a large mirror with a golden frame hanging on the wall above the fireplace. As she looked up, she saw herself reflected in that mirror and was filled with shame.\par
Then, the duke looked into the mirror and locked eyes with her. They were the same blue eyes that she had seen countless times before, and yet now they felt different and unfamiliar. And so, even as she quaked with trepidation, she didn\rquote t avoid his gaze.\par
She continued to gaze into his eyes for a long time, all the while wondering why she didn\rquote t feel compelled to look away. They looked pure and innocent.\par
He let out a self-deprecating snicker and shifted his gaze back to her bruised shoulder.\par
His body felt hot, and his lips were starting to feel dry. Only when he looked back up and saw her in the mirror again did he realize that he had been the one to avert his eyes, not her. It was the first time that this had happened in all the years he had known her.\par
Damn it\'85 he thought, while his body continued to heat up. He felt like sighing, but instead, he lowered his head towards her shoulder and kissed it.\par
\par
Perhaps he had done this to rid himself of the strange feelings welling up inside him. Perhaps he had done it to soothe her wounds. Either way, it wasn\rquote t the type of thing he would normally do, but he didn\rquote t care.\par
As she struggled to try to move her body away from him, he softly whispered in her ear, \ldblquote It\rquote s all right.\rdblquote  His voice didn\rquote t sound like it usually did. It was softer and more passionate.\par
Unable to stand to look in the mirror anymore, she quickly averted her eyes. She then saw his large hand holding her bare waist. She tried to wriggle out of his grip, but it was no use. He firmly grasped her hand and carefully continued to kiss her body.\par
She shut her eyes.\par
His lips and breath against her aching wounds felt as soft as a feather.\par
