After several peaceful days, Layla\rquote s memories of that night had grown hazy, as if it had been no more than a dream.\par
Marquess Lindman had gone back to his own estate, and Matthias had not sent any coercive notes or shown up at the cottage.\par
Meanwhile, the season had also shifted.\par
Layla opened the window and was immediately greeted by a cold breeze full of the scents of winter. She let the breeze wash over her for a moment, not worrying about how cold it was. She looked out at Arvis\rquote s forest, which was permeated with winter\rquote s distinctive silver-white sunshine.\par
As her fingers started to get cold, she closed the window and turned around. The children from her school were putting on a benefit performance at the public hall downtown today, so it took her a bit longer than usual to get ready. Even though the children were the ones who would be on stage, many\par
\par
of the region\rquote s most important VIPs would be in attendance, so she needed to look her best so she could make a good impression.\par
\ldblquote Please try to look like a dignified teacher. All right, Miss Llewellyn?\rdblquote  the principal had said at the previous day\rquote s meeting, adding that he hoped she wouldn\rquote t ride her bicycle to the benefit.\par
\ldblquote What\rquote s wrong with my bike?\rdblquote  she muttered as she braided her hair. After a full semester\rquote s worth of practice, she was able to braid her hair very neatly with ease.\par
She finished braiding her hair and admired her work in the mirror. Suddenly, her memory flashed back to what the duke had said that beautiful autumn day on Platanus Road: \ldblquote That hairstyle doesn\rquote t suit you\rdblquote  She flinched as if she were face-to-face with the real duke and turned away from the mirror.\par
Then she recalled what he had said about her hairstyle a short while later: \ldblquote It\rquote s pretty. It\rquote s like a bird\rquote s wings.\rdblquote This comment had flustered her even more than the criticism preceding it. He had uttered it with a blank expression.\par
She fiddled with her comb for a while, then looked in the mirror again. Her bruises had mostly faded away by now, but she still remembered certain things from that night clearly.\par
The duke had kept his promise. It had felt strange when he had kissed her wounds, but before long, he had stopped, and proceeded to calmly dress them. Showing as much careful delicacy as a doctor treating a patient, he had rubbed ointment on the bruises and gently wrapped a bandage around her tender shoulder.\par
Just as her mind was arriving at the point in her memories when she had put her blouse back on and faced him, she quickly stood up and got the dress and high-heeled shoes she had saved up to buy and put them on. I can\rquote t believe I\par
\par
have to wear these uncomfortable shoes all day\'85 Her heels were already aching within seconds of putting them on.\par
\ldblquote You look so pretty, Layla,\rdblquote  Bill said when she appeared in the kitchen. \ldblquote You\rquote re going to be the prettiest lady at the public hall tonight.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I don\rquote t know, Uncle Bill, there are going to be lots of noblewomen in attendance\'85\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote So what? No matter what sorts of fancy jewelry they have on, they won\rquote t compare to you.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I\rquote m glad you think so,\rdblquote  she said, giggling as she sat down across from him. \ldblquote Oh, Layla. You know that, uh\'85 that necklace? How about wearing it\par
tonight?\rdblquote  he asked, looking at her unadorned neck. \ldblquote Necklace? Ah! The necklace you got me?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Yeah. You wore it to the party at the duke\rquote s mansion last year. I think it would match the outfit you have on right? I\rquote m not saying you have to wear it, but I certainly wouldn\rquote t mind if you did.\rdblquote\par
Bill knew nothing about women\rquote s fashion, but he vividly remembered how dazzlingly beautiful Layla had looked the night of the party. She had looked like a princess, even if only for one night, and he cherished the memory.\par
Gladly taking his suggestion, Layla went back to her room, dug deep into her closet to find the necklace, and returned to the kitchen with it on. \ldblquote How do I look, Uncle Bill?\rdblquote  she asked, standing before him with her hands behind her back.\par
He chuckled. \ldblquote Be careful of crows, Layla. You\rquote re sparkling so brightly, I\rquote m worried one of them is going to snatch you away in its beak!\rdblquote\par
