\ldblquote Did you see, Miss Llewellyn? Duke Herhardt is here!\rdblquote  Mrs. Graeber whispered excitedly.\par
Layla, who had just come out into the lobby after watching the children\rquote s dress rehearsal, reacted with surprise. \ldblquote Did you say the duke? Not just his mother and grandmother?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Yes! Duke Herhardt himself! I think he came with his grandmother\'85 Ah!\par
Look over there.\rdblquote\par
Layla looked in the direction Mrs. Graeber was pointing, and saw the duke with a crowd of people surrounding him. Just then, he turned his head and made eye contact with her. She gasped, then quickly smiled and nodded before lowering her head. Thankfully, the duke walked away before too long.\par
Watching him with disappointment as he walked away, Mrs. Graeber asked Layla, \ldblquote Since you live at Arvis, do you see the duke around the estate\par
\par
now and then?\rdblquote\par
Feeling a pang of guilt, Layla clasped her hands together. \ldblquote Um\'85 yes, occasionally.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Wow! I\rquote m jealous. I would be so happy to be able to see him occasionally, even if it were very infrequently and from a great distance.\rdblquote\par
Ever since the school field trip to Arvis that autumn, Mrs. Graeber had been showing limitless admiration for the duke. She continued to gush forth to Layla about him\emdash how elegant and kind he was, and thus how great of a nobleman he was. Eventually, she went back into the auditorium to attend to the upper-class children\rquote s choir rehearsal, which she was in charge of.\par
Layla was passing through the lobby to meet with some of the other teachers when she saw Duke Herhardt again. Looking highly dignified, he was talking to a middle-aged gentleman. She stopped walking for a moment and cautiously watched him.\par
Ever since she was young, she had always felt scared and uncomfortable around the duke. Thus, it had always felt strange to her when others heaped praise on him. She was usually unable to agree with what they said about him, but she had never felt compelled to find out why they liked him so much.\par
She still felt this way, although she at least no longer thought their compliments of him were mere empty praise. They were right; he was perfectly carrying out his role as Duke Matthias von Herhardt, lord of Arvis. This made his hidden personality, which only she knew, feel like something from a dream, a beautiful but brutal nightmare, to be exact.\par
She slowly started raising her gaze again from the long shadow she was casting on the lobby\rquote s marble floor. It struck her how tall he was. He had a slender frame, but seeing him in front of her, she was almost overcome by how strong he looked.\par
\par
And his blue eyes\'85 Wait, she thought, his eyes? She realized that he was looking at her out of the corner of his eye, even as he remained facing the person he was talking to. Wondering why he was looking at her, she looked back at him in a daze. His eyes were showing no particular emotion, but there was a subtle grin on his lips.\par
\ldblquote What are you doing here, Miss Llewellyn?\rdblquote\par
Layla jumped at the sound of the principal\rquote s voice behind her. \ldblquote I\rquote m sorry if I startled you. Come now, let\rquote s go greet everyone.\rdblquote\par
The principal then started walking with the rest of the teachers towards the area where Duke Herhardt was standing with Dowager Herhardt. Somehow, Layla ended up at the front of the pack, near the duke.\par
Matthias\rquote s gaze moved over all the teachers, and ended up on Layla. Before she lowered her eyes, she caught a glimpse of a slight smile in his narrowed eyes. She wondered why he would be smiling, but she didn\rquote t want to look up. Instead, she just stared at his well-polished shoes, wishing that the performance would start soon.\par
Little did she know the troubles that she was going to face that night.\par
