Hesitating to reply to his request for a second date, she nervously looked around again. Just then, she heard the sound of a car approaching from behind them. Her heart sank. She wanted to believe she was imagining it, but the sound continued to grow louder.\par
Soon, the dusky road was illuminated by the car\rquote s headlights. The car slowed down slightly as it passed them, then sped up again. It was Duke Herhardt\rquote s car.\par
\ldblquote Miss Llewellyn?\rdblquote\par
The sound of the young man\rquote s voice snapped her out of her daze. \ldblquote I\rquote m sorry,\rdblquote  she said, lowering her head. \lquote 1\'85 don\rquote t think I\rquote m ready for that kind of relationship yet. I\rquote m really sorry.\rdblquote\par
\par
She had agreed to have tea with the young man at the principal\rquote s urging, but she had absolutely no intention of looking for a potential husband at the moment. Perhaps she would get married someday, but for the time being, she just wanted to work hard and live an ordinary life.\par
\ldblquote Oh\'85 I see.\rquote  He couldn\rquote t hide his disappointment at her firm rejection, but he understood how she felt and respected it. He told her that he was the one who should be apologizing, not her. He hoped that he hadn\rquote t made her too uncomfortable by pressing her for a second date. After telling her this, he walked off with a sullen look on his face.\par
She felt bad for hurting him when he was clearly a good person, but she knew she had made the right choice. If she had failed to reject him early on, it could only led to him getting hurt more deeply later on, just like what had happened with Kyle.\par
She winced at the sudden thought of Kyle. She often wondered how he was doing, and she also realized that all she could do for him was pray that he was doing well. No matter how much she missed him, there was no going back to their days together, when they used to walk down this very road together, laughing and chatting.\par
After the young man left, she remained standing in the same spot until the road was completely dark. This was because, as soon as she stopped thinking about how much she missed the good old days with Kyle, her mind was flooded with uneasiness. She worried that if she walked any farther down the road, she might run into the duke. She was suddenly reminded of that strange, first autumn that the duke had stayed at Arvis.\par
She took a slow, deep breath of the cold winter air, and tried to picture the coming spring when she would be starting a new chapter in a new place.\par
\par
She hoped to find a place to stay that had a huge window. If her room got a lot of sunlight, maybe she wouldn\rquote t be too sad. Ideally, there would be a tree outside the window that she could look at, or if not, at least a nearby park or forest she could visit when she missed the smell of Arvis\rquote s lush vegetation.\par
Eventually, these thoughts about the happy days to come calmed her anxious heart. Feeling a little braver, she cautiously walked her bicycle down the road. After turning a corner, she was happy to see that Platanus Road was filled with nothing but the white moonlight and the black shadows of the trees lining it.\par
She breathed a sigh of relief, then nimbly jumped up onto the seat of her bicycle. The sound of her energetic pedaling filled the silence of the night.\par
