When Layla didn\rquote t move, a menacing look swept over the officer\rquote s face.\par
Chef Mona hurried over and pulled Layla aside.\par
\ldblquote Uncle Bill!\rdblquote  Layla shouted as she watched Bill being practically crammed into the police car.\par
Bill urgently gestured for her to step back while he continued to wear a forced smile. \ldblquote Go and wait for me at home! I\rquote ll be there soon, don\rquote t worry. Got it? Oh, and Layla\'85\rdblquote\par
He seemed like he had something more to say, but the officers were out of patience. They shoved him into the back seat and slammed the door shut, then\par
\par
departed from Arvis, leaving Layla behind, crying.\par
