Don \rquote t cry, she told herself.\par
Throughout the long, dreadful night, she had not cried once. She certainly wasn\rquote t going to let herself cry now.\par
Before long, she heard the sound of the bedroom door closing, and then the sound of the cabin\rquote s front door opening and closing. He was finally gone.\par
Only then did she sit up. She rubbed her swollen lips and saw that they were a little bloody. It stung, but it was a fairly minor wound.\par
\par
She cautiously got out of bed and was suddenly confronted with her own image. It took her a moment before she realized she was looking into the mirror above the mantelpiece.\par
Ignoring the urge to look away, she stared at herself for a long while. It was just another meaningless night with a man who means nothing to me, she thought. Unfortunately, the pain lingering in her body wasn\rquote t easy to ignore.\par
Feeling too dirty to get dressed right away, she took a handkerchief from the pocket of her coat and wiped off her body. She had to stop a few times to calm her breathing, but she didn\rquote t cry. She was proud of herself for that.\par
