\par
\ldblquote So, Captain Herhardt,\rdblquote  Riette said, sitting up, \ldblquote having spent time on the overseas war front, what\rquote s your opinion on all this? If a full-scale war breaks out, do you think the general consensus that we would win is correct?\rdblquote\par
Matthias finally turned to look at them and replied, \ldblquote It wouldn\rquote t be easy.\rdblquote  It was a dismal response, but his face and tone were infused with optimism. \ldblquote If it were just a war between Berg and Lovita, we\rquote d have a high chance of winning, but once war broke out, it would likely expand to other countries.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Yes, that\rquote s true,\rdblquote  the crown prince replied, letting out a worried sigh.\par
The tension between the continent\rquote s various kingdoms was mounting day by day. As Riette had pointed out, tracing back the family lines of the continent\rquote s ruling families would reveal that they all had blood ties to each other. However, war couldn\rquote t necessarily be avoided for such a sentimental reason. There were just too many overlapping interests. The countries of the continent were interconnected by so many alliances and treaties if two countries went to war against each other, it would quickly escalate into a full- scale continental war.\par
\ldblquote You don\rquote t need to worry so much, Your Highness. People have had these same concerns since our fathers\rquote  fathers\rquote  generation, but the concerns never turned into reality. Even if our generation is not so lucky and full-scale war does break out, well, that\rquote s just an opportunity for us to become war heroes.\rdblquote\par
Riette\rquote s quip made the crown prince smile. \ldblquote I suppose you\rquote re right. But please, Riette, stop with the \lquote Your Highness\rquote  nonsense. Talk to me like you normally do. The formality makes me feel tense\rdblquote\par
