\par
The crown prince chuckled, and Riette broke into laughter as well. They had gotten along together like this since they were children. As time went on, each of them ascended to his own position of power, but the dynamic of their friendship never really changed.\par
Matthias watched the two others laughing like little boys, then shifted his gaze out the window. It was late morning. Suddenly he saw Layla heading out on an outing somewhere. She was wearing a nice outfit. She looked pretty. Pretty enough to make him momentarily forget their upsetting last conversation.\par
He scoffed at the thought of a mistress who couldn\rquote t even appreciate a gift. If the point of a mistress was a pleasure, then Layla Llewellyn was a dreadful mistress. In spite of this, he had no desire to get rid of her. He didn\rquote t know why this was, nor did he care to know.\par
He had desired her for a long time, and now he had her. That was that.\par
Even if she hated him, even if she found him creepy, she was his.\par
She\rquote s mine, he thought. Smiling again, he picked up his teacup. My little bird. He thought of her downy, golden hair fluttering as she writhed beneath him. The better he had gotten to know her body, the more beautifully she had\par
sung for him.\par
It had been several days since he had heard that moaning song of hers. As he realized this, his grip on the teacup in his hand tightened. He didn\rquote t understand how he had become so consumed by desire, but he had.\par
Ever since the first night that their bodies had been entangled on the cabin\rquote s drawing-room floor, all his senses had been attuned to her. The slightest hint of her would fog his mind and make his body feel hot. In such moments, she became the whole world to him. He enjoyed thinking of her so much he didn\rquote t want to stop.\par
\par
My beautiful little bird.\par
By now, he had no difficulty covering his canary\rquote s eyes and clipping its little wings. As the clipped feathers fluttered to the floor, he would take the cloth off of its eyes, and it would shake its body briefly. After flapping its clipped wings, it would turn its clear, innocent eyes towards its master again and sing.\par
Sometimes at such moments, Matthias had the sudden urge to crush the bird in his hand, so that its life would end while it was singing its most beautiful song, just for him, and he could cherish the moment forever.\par
Sometimes he had a similar feeling while he was with Layla. When she wasn\rquote t rejecting him, wasn\rquote t trying to get away, but was writhing along with his movements, letting out a cry that only he could hear, in such moments he wished that time could stop and allow him to savor the feeling forever.\par
When he watched her squirming underneath him, with her eyes unfocused and her whole body flushed red, he sometimes found the sight so beautiful that he felt like strangling her. When she got swept up by instinctual pleasure and wrapped her limbs around him while moaning sweetly, he sometimes wished that he could devour her from head to toe.\par
\ldblquote Matthias?\rquote\rquote\par
He turned around at the sound of his name and saw Riette, with the crown prince standing next to him. When he saw the servants waiting in front of the open door, he realized that his mind had been elsewhere for a long while. It wasn\rquote t a great position to be in.\par
He set down his teacup and stood up as if nothing had happened. It was time to start getting ready for dinner.\par
Before leaving the study, he impulsively turned to look out the window one last time. He wondered if Layla had returned home yet. He laughed at\par
\par
himself in his mind for harping on such thoughts, when he knew full well that she had nowhere else to go in this world.\par
He turned around, trying to drive the idle thoughts out of his mind. He managed to walk down the hallway, which was fully of the mellow light of the setting sun, without thinking of her. However, once he reached his bedroom, her name popped into his head again.\par
Layla.\par
He had her, and yet he had the strange, unsettling feeling that she wasn\rquote t wholly his.\par
What if she doesn\rquote t come back? He ruminated on this worry as he changed his clothes. It didn\rquote t matter that he knew she would never leave her beloved uncle Bill Remmer behind and run away. He was still worried. Would she leave me\'85? Midway through fastening his cufflinks, his hands suddenly froze. The emotion he was feeling at the prospect of her leaving him was less like anger or anxiety than perplexity. The thought seemed ridiculous and absurd. A day without the sun or a night without stars seemed more likely.\par
\ldblquote Um, Your Grace\'85?\rquote  his assistant cautiously said.\par
Matthias finished fastening his cufflinks and turned around. While his assistant brushed off his evening jacket, he calmly looked at his reflection in the mirror and thought back to the first time he had clipped his canary\rquote s wings. That time, he had clipped the feathers too deeply. As a result, the wing had bled, and the bird had recoiled in pain. However, the bleeding had quickly stopped, and the bird was fine after that.\par
After that poor, beautiful bird was rendered flightless, he had cherished it even more. It was also only after having its wings clipped that it started eagerly approaching its master and singing. Even when its feathers grew back, it never tried to fly away. His bird loved its cage, and it loved him.\par
\par
He stepped out of the dressing room into his bedroom and walked up to the birdcage. Sitting on its perch, the bird cocked its head and looked at him.\par
If you could never fly away, I could pamper you even more. I could give you a great Use. You wouldn\rquote t need a cage. I could give you so many things to enjoy.\par
\ldblquote It\rquote s time, Your Grace,\rdblquote  his assistant said, looking at his watch.\par
Matthias nodded and looked out the window. The trees were casting long shadows on the dusky road. Layla was still nowhere in sight.\par
