After a five-day stay, the crown prince and his retinue were finally going to leave. All of the Arvis staff members lined up in front of the mansion to bid them farewell. Just as with the welcome ceremony, Layla was at the very end of the line. She wasn\rquote t going to miss the increased security that she had had to\par
\par
deal with whenever she entered Arvis during the crown prince\rquote s stay. But still, she was disappointed that the visit was coming to an end.\par
Throughout the entire visit, the duke had not had her meet him at the cabin a single time. It was as if he had forgotten about her entirely. Thanks to this, she had been able to enjoy several days of peace, just like the old days. It was as if she were nothing more than Mr. Remmer\rquote s daughter.\par
Maybe\'85 he\rquote s over me, she suddenly thought. This optimistic prospect made her heart start pounding.\par
As she thought about it, it occurred to her that it had been a ridiculous infatuation from the start. He had probably only wanted her because he couldn\rquote t accept that there was something in the world he couldn\rquote t have. Yes, she was sure of that now. By now, he had probably enjoyed her enough that she was no longer any fun for him. And how long could such an arrogant man stand being with a woman who hated him? Probably not long.\par
This is wonderful she whispered to herself. It was then that the duke looked over his shoulder. Before she had time to react, their eyes met. It was only for a brief moment, but it was long enough for each of them to recognize that they were looking at each other.\par
She got a strange feeling and immediately lowered her eyes. After a moment, she peeked up again. The duke was facing away from her, bidding farewell to the crown prince. Claudine was standing next to him.\par
After the farewell ceremony concluded and the crown prince and his retinue departed from Arvis, the duke escorted Claudine into the mansion. Sighs of relief could be heard from staff members all over.\par
\ldblquote I think it was a mistake for them to postpone the wedding. Just look\emdash  Miss Claudine already looks like a duchess,\rdblquote  a nearby maid whispered.\par
\par
While the other maids were voicing their agreement, Layla turned around and left.\par
As she reached the forest path leading back to the cottage, her heart started beating faster. The mere thought that she might soon be free of that man made her feel like shackles had been removed from her ankles.\par
Once the duke got married, she wanted to leave Arvis with Uncle Bill and move somewhere far away, far enough for the duke to forget about them. Once there, they could have a fresh start at life. She didn\rquote t mind if they would never be able to go back to the life they had led before. She would just have to try as hard as she could, and then maybe the nightmare that the duke had created for her would turn into a distant memory.\par
Excited by this hopeful thought, she moved faster and more confidently than usual. After doing the laundry and cleaning the house, she baked some jam cookies. There had been a special one- day-only sale on flour, so she had bought a large quantity of it Carrying such a heavy load home in the cold had been quite hard, but she forgot all the effort when she pulled the baking sheet of perfectly-browned cookies out of the oven.\par
She had a leisurely day at the cottage. After eating a whole plateful of the cookies she had baked, she read a book for a while, and then responded to some letters that friends had sent her. Just as she was sealing the last letter in an envelope, she heard a loud, friendly voice outside.\par
\ldblquote Layla!\rdblquote  It was her kind, chatty neighbor Chef Mona.\par
\ldblquote Yes, Chef Mona!\rdblquote  she replied, running to the front door to greet her.\par
Whenever there had been a big party at the mansion, Mona would always come to the cottage carrying a huge basket full of leftover food. Today was no different.\par
\par
Stepping into the kitchen, she took a deep breath of the sweet, cookie- scented air and smiled. \ldblquote With Bill still out of town, I was worried if you were eating enough, but I see that you\rquote re now a mature young woman.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote It\rquote s all thanks to you, Chef Mona,\rdblquote  Layla replied, taking the basket and setting it down on the table. While she made tea, Mona sat down and looked around the kitchen.\par
It was Mona who had taught Layla how to cook. From the time when Layla was a little girl with tiny hands, she followed Mona\rquote s instruction so well that it didn\rquote t take long for her to become a skilled homemaker. The cottage\rquote s kitchen had been a source of delicious meals ever since.\par
With tea and sweet treats on the table between them, Layla and Mona sat and chatted like normal. Mona did most of the talking, while Layla mostly smiled and nodded.\par
\ldblquote You did a great job with these cookies! I think you\rquote re ready to get married now,\rdblquote  Mona exclaimed with some slight exaggeration. \lquote Oh, Layla, while we\rquote re on the subject, did you and Kyle end up-\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I\rquote ve gotten good at baking cakes, too, Chef Mona,\rdblquote  Layla quickly said, cutting Mona off before she could change the subject. \ldblquote Next time I make one, I\rquote d like you to taste it and critique my work\rdblquote  Her tone was so serious you\rquote d think that cake baking was the most important thing in the world.\par
\ldblquote I\rquote ll be sure to pay you a visit next time you make one!\rdblquote  Mona said. She was disappointed that Layla didn\rquote t want to talk about Kyle, but she decided not to press her on it. Ever since Kyle had returned to Karlsbar, all of the Arvis staff had been wondering about him and Layla. Even so, she didn\rquote t want to reopen an old wound for her.\par
Instead, she started telling Layla all about the busy week she had had cooking for not only the crown prince and princess, but all the fastidious\par
\par
aristocrats that came to see them as well. It was clear from her heated tone that she had a lot of built-up irritation. \ldblquote And just when I thought I\rquote d finally be getting a break, I heard that Lady Claudine is staying here. What\rquote s with that? Why does she need to stay at Arvis when her fiance will be gone?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote The duke left again?\rdblquote  Layla cautiously asked.\par
After eating two cookies in a row, Mona casually nodded. \ldblquote Yeah. What was it for again? I think a business matter came up. Anyway, he\rquote s going to have to spend a few days in a neighboring city taking care of it. After the crown prince left this morning, the duke had a quick lunch and then left right away.\rdblquote\par
Layla\rquote s face started to flush with excitement.\par
Mona didn\rquote t know what she was so excited about, but rather than dwelling on it, she continued talking. \ldblquote So anyway, Lady Claudine is staying at Arvis while he\rquote s away. They say it\rquote s so that she can discuss wedding plans with the duke\rquote s mom and grandma, but I think that\rquote s just an excuse those women made up because they adore her and want to spend more time with her. But now I\rquote m in the hot seat. I\rquote ve never cooked for such a picky eater!\rdblquote\par
After getting her frustrations thoroughly off her chest, Mona left the cottage.\par
Layla locked the windows and door, then returned to the kitchen table and sat down. There was still a cookie left on Mona\rquote s plate. She picked it up and took a bite. The sound of her chewing filled the silent kitchen.\par
The relief she felt at the prospect of more peaceful days ahead was just as sweet as the taste of the cookie. I\rquote m so happy, she thought, wiping the crumbs from her mouth with the back of her hand.\par
This is wonderful.\par
