Just as Matthias wanted, he and Layla spent an ordinary, uneventful day together.\par
She kept her head down as if she were embarrassed to look at him. Feeling very relaxed, he watched her as she ate her breakfast. Observing the meticulous care with which she chewed and swallowed each bite, he thought to himself. How Layla-like of her. He snickered at himself for thinking such a corny thought, but he wasn\rquote t ashamed.\par
Feeling his gaze, she furtively lifted her head. There was a guarded expression on her face, but the breadcrumbs on her lips made her look harmless. At first, he pretended not to notice, then he took pity and pointed to the left side of her mouth. Tilling her head, she cautiously touched the spot, then started blushing when felt the crumbs. He watched this with great amusement.\par
Flustered, she wiped the crumbs away with her napkin, then continued eating. Noticing the care with which she tapped her spoon against her boiled egg and peeled away its shell, he once again thought to himself, How Layla-like of her. This made him chuckle.\par
After removing the whole shell, she looked up at him with a puzzled expression. She hesitated for a moment, then cautiously took a bite and started chewing. This made him laugh even more loudly.\par
Breakfast was followed by some leisurely free time.\par
\par
Of course, it was only leisurely for him. She spent the time anxiously pacing around the room. He suspected that she was trying to show him how uncomfortable she was being in his presence, but he didn\rquote t mind. He just enjoyed having her with him.\par
He went to settle the bill. When he returned, she was sitting by the window, reading the newspaper that he had left on the coffee table. She was so engrossed in what she was reading, she didn\rquote t notice him approaching.\par
Feeling very curious to know what she was reading, he peeked over her shoulder. To his surprise, she was reading an installment of a serialized mystery novel. It was a part of the newspaper that he had never looked at.\par
When she finally sensed his presence behind her, she flinched and dropped the newspaper, which fell to the floor between them.\par
To think that someone with such an innocent-looking face enjoyed reading gory novels about criminals! He burst into laughter at the thought.\par
She stared at him like he was crazy.\par
Maybe she\rquote s right. Maybe I am crazy, he thought. So be it..\par
They left the hotel shortly before noon. She protested, but he remained firm in his decision. His assistant brought a second coat for him. Putting that one on himself, he draped his own coat over her shoulders. It was so big on her, it almost dragged on the ground as she walked. He found the sight of this adorable.\par
\ldblquote Where are we going?\rdblquote  she nervously asked as they stepped out of the hotel\rquote s front entrance.\par
Rather than saying anything in response, he simply started walking towards the place his assistant had told him about. As they arrived in front of the clothing store, her face went stiff. \ldblquote This isn\rquote t necessary,\rdblquote  she said, frowning and shaking her head.\par
