As they reached the park, he held out his arm for her. Unsure of the reason for the gesture, she just stared at his arm Her cheeks quickly reddened With a serious look on her face, she looked around. She was stuck between a rock and a hard place.\par
It was quite an irritating attitude, but he didn\rquote t feel particularly bothered by it. Deciding to respect her wishes, he grabbed her hand and started walking again. She tried desperately to wrest her hand away from his, until he firmly interlocked his fingers with hers, at which point she gave up.\par
After a leisurely walk, they went to a cafe and took their seats in front of a large window overlooking the entrance to the park. He gazed at her with his head aslant. When she was with others, such as Bill Remmer, she seemed fairly talkative, but with him, she rarely opened her mouth.\par
He looked out the window and noticed a bird sitting in a tree by the street. \ldblquote What kind of bird is that?\rdblquote  he asked, pointing to it.\par
Surprised by his question, she looked up and saw the bird he was pointing at. \ldblquote It\rquote s a raven,\rdblquote  she replied. How can he not know what a raven looks like?\par
She couldn\rquote t believe it. Even little children knew what ravens looked like.\par
And there were plenty of them in Arvis\rquote s forest.\par
