Kyle remained in his seat long after Claudine had left the cafe. The waiter quietly approached and set down the third cup of coffee for him before taking away the cold second cup, which Kyle hadn\rquote t even touched. The afternoon sunlight was warm, but Kyle\rquote s face was white as a sheet as he sat\par
staring into space.\par
Don\rquote t get swept up in Claudine\rquote s lies, he had told himself repeatedly during their meeting. He was sure that she was making everything up in order to slander Layla. If it wasn\rquote t that, it didn\rquote t make any sense. How could Layla do such things?\par
However, despite his best efforts, doubt was already starting to eat away at him as he thought back to the strange uneasiness he had recently felt whenever he had seen Layla and the duke together.\par
If she\rquote s really the duke\rquote s mistress\'85 then what are she and I?\par
\par
Claudine had said that Layla\rquote s relationship with the duke had begun immediately after Kyle had left for the capital. Almost as if they had been waiting for the chance. Claudine hadn\rquote t made much of an attempt to hide her malice as she had said this, and he had already wondered if it was all a ruse. Now, however, he wondered if those slanderous words she had uttered were true.\par
He didn\rquote t know Claudine well, but there was one thing about her of which he was certain. No matter how much she disliked Layla, she wouldn\rquote t harm her own reputation just to slander her. She had too much self-pride for that.\par
That dyed-in-the-wool aristocrat wouldn\rquote t disgrace herself and her fiance just to hurt Layla, would she? \lquote No,\rdblquote  he muttered, shaking his head to rid himself of the suspicion. This isn\rquote t just anyone, it\rquote s Layla.\par
He staggered up from his seat and left the busy cafe. There was a cold breeze, but his mind remained cloudy. Without knowing where he was headed, he started walking down the sidewalk with an uneven gait. His eyes were welling up with tears, but he just kept walking. He soon found himself unable to breathe properly.\par
In his head, he grasped what Claudine had told him, but his heart wouldn\rquote t believe it. As this discrepancy started to make him feel like he was being torn up inside, he collapsed to the ground in from of an empty alleyway and clutched his head.\par
He had to see Layla. He knew that was the only way. But what could he possibly say to her?\par
Feeling even more lost, he shut his eyes.\par
