Matthias and Layla had what could almost be called a normal conversation For the most part, he asked questions and she answered them, but occasionally she would pose small questions to him as well. He didn\rquote t mind that she only seemed to be asking them out of politeness.\par
She was facing him without fear or anger, listening to his questions and responding to them. He didn\rquote t care what the reason was. She had a gentle expression on her face, and her large eyes were looking straight at him.\par
He paid close attention to every little thing she said, and to every slight shift in her posture or facial expression. As he did, he felt a strange, warm feeling in his chest. All he was doing was quietly gazing at her, yet his breathing was growing shaky. He felt oddly nervous.\par
Have I gone mad? he wondered, just as he had wondered earlier that morning. And yet, he felt utterly satisfied in that moment. It was enough for him.\par
\ldblquote Are we leaving now?\rdblquote  she cautiously asked, unable to hide her eagerness as she saw him checking his watch.\par
\ldblquote Sure,\rdblquote  he calmly replied, setting aside his pathetic, sentimental wish that their time together would continue forever.\par
She looked down and quietly exhaled. It bothered him that she seemed so relieved at the news that they were leaving, but he still couldn\rquote t take his eyes off her.\par
\par
His throat was dry, and he felt almost feverish. He fervently wished that she would look at him again. As if she had heard his wish, she hesitantly looked up at him. She had been chewing on her lower lip, so it shone with a deep red.\par
\ldblquote You\rquote re\'85 going to keep the secret, right?\rdblquote  she asked. \ldblquote The secret?\rdblquote\par
