Oh, that\rquote s right, he thought as she reminded him of the reason why she was here in front of him. It was because of his threat or his advice. Whichever it was, hearing her whisper her uncle\rquote s name made him feel awful.\par
When he wouldn\rquote t give a firm answer, she said with greater urgency, \ldblquote He can never know anything about this.\rdblquote\par
Bill Remmer\'85 As he repeated that name in his mind, his blue eyes regained their usual coldness. What could be so great about him that she is ready to give away everything she has for him?\par
\ldblquote Even if I keep the secret, do you really think he will remain in the dark about us forever?\rdblquote  he sincerely asked.\par
No secret could last forever. Especially this sort of secret. However, she just stared at him uncomprehendingly.\par
\ldblquote Forever\'85?\rdblquote  she finally asked, furrowing her brow at his puzzling question.\par
At the longest, their relationship would last only until the duke\rquote s wedding In the summer. Even If he still showed interest in her after that, she was determined to sever ties with him. And yet he was now talking about forever. Her hands started shaking under the table. She couldn\rquote t believe he would use such a grand word in talking about their relationship.\par
\par
After taking a sip of water, he set down his glass and coldly said, \ldblquote He\rquote s going to find out eventually\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote No!\rdblquote  she shouted, thinking, I\rquote m going to get away from you before that car happen. To stop herself from expressing that sentiment to him out loud, she forcefully bit her lip, then said, \ldblquote D- don\rquote t say that, all right? Uncle Bill c-can\rquote t know anything about us.\rdblquote\par
She didn\rquote t like that she was pleading with a man who was using cowardly tricks on her, but she knew she had to. She couldn\rquote t stand the thought of letting Uncle Bill get hurt. He wouldn\rquote t be able to stand it if he were to find out the shameful deal she had made with the duke. Thus, her relationship with the duke needed to stay a secret until the day that she could escape the duke\rquote s grasp. She was willing to do anything towards that end, even if it meant enduring all sorts of indignities as he treated her like his plaything.\par
\ldblquote Your Grace,\rdblquote  she said, her voice shaking as it always did when she made this sort of plea, \ldblquote please.\rdblquote\par
As he looked into her eyes, which were filled with a mixture of fear and expectancy, a twisted smile formed on his lips.\par
She was beautiful. He had wanted to have her. So, he had made her his. His eyes slowly narrowed as he looked at her. Made her mine\'85 ? Suddenly he questioned this idea. Was she really his?\par
Her dream of marrying another man and departing had been crushed, leaving her stuck at Arvis. Ultimately she had become his mistress. Everything had gone according to his wishes.\par
He nodded to agree to her request. He didn\rquote t tell her that it was only a matter of time before the gardener would find out about their relationship, but he knew it was true. He himself didn\rquote t understand why he couldn\rquote t let go of this woman who by all accounts should have meant nothing to him. He didn\rquote t\par
\par
